    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py` and the 51 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. The implementation covers every rule in `spec.md`: dest validation with trailing-slash stripping, `/` and `\\` as separators, dropping empty and `.` segments, `..` handling that rejects any climb above the destination, and rejection of NUL, absolute paths, drive prefixes and empty results. Directory entries are validated but left out of the result, and case-insensitive duplicates are rejected. Any unsafe member raises before anything is returned, so there is never a partial plan. I did not run a coverage tool because only the test command was permitted. By reading the code, every line and branch of `solution.py` is exercised by the tests, so the 90% gate should pass. One test I wrote first was wrong: `a:b` starts with a letter followed by `:`, so the spec treats it as a drive prefix. I changed that test to `ab:c`, which is an ordinary name.",
